# nr-office-ooxml-docx-edits: integration fragment

Two modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): docx_edits (the body, table, comment and story edits of
portable-docx-edits.mjs) and docx (the Word batch of portable-docx.mjs: `apply_docx`). No protocol method, service, Cargo
dependency or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to this task: every crate they use (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-fonts,
mixdog-office-base, and mixdog-ooxml's own modules docx_parts, docx_xml, docx_operations, docx_tracked_edits, docx_runs,
docx_formatting, docx_styles, snapshot_docx, template_tokens, opc, text_metrics and xml) is already a dependency or a module of
mixdog-ooxml; the twin test uses base64, tempfile and mixdog-fonts, which are already dependencies of the crate.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After the line `pub mod docx_operations;` add:

    pub mod docx_edits;
    pub mod docx;

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-docx-operations (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-edits.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-docx-edits/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "0a36f30f0992a2ca801cfad6bea6673d130c1c985437bc0e55cf58677107187a",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-edits.mjs",
      "set": "office-docx-edits",
      "totalBytes": 573954
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-docx-edits/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that keeps
this file reorders or reformats them.)

## For the tasks that call a Word batch

The entry point is `mixdog_ooxml::docx::apply_docx(proof, measurer, zip, operations)`: `proof` is the read proof that reads the
pictures an add_image operation names, `measurer` the `TextMeasurer` that sizes a table that names no widths, `zip` the
`Package`, `operations` the batch's `&[serde_json::Value]`; it answers the result rows (one per operation) or the message of the
operation that failed (what the operations before it changed stays in the package, as in Node). The same module re-exports
`refresh_docx_table_of_contents`. The edits themselves are `mixdog_ooxml::docx_edits::*` under the Node names in snake case
(`DocxContext { parts, tracking }` carries the story part list and the track-changes state to the edits that read them). The
operation names the dispatcher serves are the keys of `DOCUMENT_EDITS` of portable-docx.mjs plus `track_changes`; any other name
(an inherited one such as `constructor` included) is `Portable DOCX backend does not support operation: <name>`.

## Not compiled

The two modules and tests/twin_docx_edits.rs were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): the first build,
`cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml`, is the check (rustfmt parses all three files). The twin test replays
native/core/fixtures/office-docx-edits (46 sequences recorded from Node: every operation of the batch with its error cases, track
changes carried across operations, and the repairs the dispatcher makes after a batch) and needs no Node; `twin_live_docx_edits`
(ignored) re-records through Node. The recorder needs `benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/lib/common.mjs` beside it (it is in the
integration tree; this worktree does not check `benchmarks/` out).
